  "method": "One discarded warmup per variant, then three trials in rotating variant order. Cases and MSM calls run sequentially, Rayon default 14 threads. No simultaneous task-owned benchmark/build; normal desktop apps not controlled. Factors 1,2,4 crossed with stock arkworks and test-only unsigned bounded-window Pippenger. Actual CRS bases, seeded distinct random scalar vectors with 0,1,-1 edge scalars. Same scalars across variants/trials.",
  "timed": "Precompute includes allocation, copying the original bases, repeated doubling and batch normalization. MSM includes scalar conversion/splitting, bucket computation and affine output. Total starts before precompute and ends after sequential MSM results are collected; equality assertions and table destruction are outside timing.",
  "excluded": "CRS I/O/decoding, input scalar generation and reference correctness oracle. Not whole-prover timing, captured protocol scalars, merged multi-source commitments, proof verification, E2E, CUDA or a long-lived cross-proof cache experiment.",
  "correctness": "All outputs equal stock arkworks. Separate edge tests cover zero, one, minus one, random scalars, infinity and duplicate bases for all factors and both kernels.",
  "conclusion": "No production adoption: every precompute candidate loses at the tested 3/4-use workloads. Stock factor 2 reduces warm per-MSM time by about 11% at large counts but not enough to repay precompute. Estimated 27/29 uses to repay is extrapolation, not measured long-lived workload. No claim against all other precomputation algorithms.",
